# Testing Guidelines and Best Practices

> **Note**: For one-time setup examples and conftest.py fixtures, see `conftest_examples.mdc`. This file focuses on ongoing testing patterns and practices.

## Core Testing Principles

- Use `pytest` through `uv run pytest`
- Use fixtures with pytest
- Only mock when 100% required (side effects, external systems)
- Mock the filesystem and always access files there (conftest.py)
- One assertion per test is ideal, but multiple related asserts are acceptable if they logically belong together
- Use `pytest.raises` for exceptions in parameterized tests
- Avoid unnecessary assertion messages
- Test behavior, not implementation

## Fixtures to use for testing

> **Note**: For comprehensive fixture examples and one-time setup code, see `conftest_examples.mdc`. This includes:
